Z||000011||theogre||05-11-99||09:28 PM||||I get the pic just fine. on 2 diferant machines. :P<p>it looks like the normal Fiero red, but w/o a good close up it's hard to tell. That paint code should be listed in any standard paint book from DuPont, or PPG. ((you should have written this crap down when you painted it in the states cliff,,,, you silly boy.[let me guess. someone painted it before you got it.]))<p>If you can match it. DuPont Imron might be a good choice of paint if it will stick to the plastic. Imron is a "epoxy" style polyurethane enamel paint. It uses a hardening agent. Once it's dry the damn stuff is about bullet proof. We used to paint motor cycles with it. I think we even used it on a boat once....<p>I just checked to be sure they still make it.... search dupont at  <A HREF="http://www.dupont.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dupont.com/</A>  use keyword imron for more data. If Imron will work on that surface use it. it's worth the wait.
